A||||11||Homicidal||Anybody got a guide on how to dis-assemble the headlight MOTOR?||||1||
Z||000000||Homicidal||06-08-2000||03:58 PM||||A while back I said my headlights are stuck up and I got the super loud cranking noise.  Everybody said it was due to a bad gear, and I should turn the gear around.<P>Anyways, I am going to do it, but I need a guide on howto take it apart!  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||06-08-2000||04:08 PM||||Are they the 84-86? or 87-88 motors?||||reg||1
Z||000002||ggarsk||06-08-2000||09:04 PM||||Check out this site: <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/headlight.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/headlight.htm</A>  It gives a good description of what to do.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||06-08-2000||09:20 PM||||   Rodney Dickman has the instructions and the parts you'll need once you get it open and realize that you need a new nylon gear.<BR> Go to <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1" TARGET=_blank>www.execpc.com/~rodney1</A>  It's $20.00 per side, I believe.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000004||Monkeyman||06-09-2000||10:48 AM||||Doug Kinney (aka the Fiero Warehouse) also carries a rebuild kit or he can rebuild yours for $45 with a core or something like $75 without.  His site says that he already has some done.||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||06-09-2000||11:10 AM||||Homicidal, Rodney's kits are something like $4.50 per side - they consist of three nylon type bushings that fit inside the gear wheel inside the motor -- I seriously doubt that both gear wheels have gone bad though -- and, it is somewhat unique that both would suddenly malfunction at the same time.......however - to rebuild the motor using the gear plugs (as I call them) is not too difficult - it took me about 30 minutes per side to remove, disassemble, reassemble and reinstall them.........||||reg||1
Z||000006||stsmithgt||06-09-2000||11:36 AM||||A 10 pound sledge would take it apart real fast  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  OOOOH  you want to rebuild it.  Never mind.||||reg||1
Z||000007||stsmithgt||06-09-2000||11:37 AM||||A 10 pound sledge would take it apart real fast  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  OOOOH  you want to rebuild it.  Never mind.  Though the sledge technique is mentally satisfying.||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||06-09-2000||12:50 PM||||I used Rodney's kit (gears and bumpers) and it was priced right and had good.<P> It took me 1 hour to do the first one and 30 minutes to do the second. <P>A vice and some large sockets are needed to press the plate off and back on to the shaft.<P>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 06-09-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 06-11-2000).]||||reg||14
